5:`$refs` is a `current` view (§8.6), so the name resolves to its current\n894:| scale indexing under covered indexes (`dao.space.index`)             | the covered-index publisher and `open-published!` are EAVT/AEVT/AVET/VAET over datoms           |\n918:| semantic             | instruction vector   | validate (§7.5), decode positional operands into the image (the `case` of `semantic.cljc:563-593` reading `(nth tuple i)`|\n921:| semantic,            | row set              | `lower` (§5.2) then the row above; composed by the composition exactly as `linearize/ast-loader` is today                |\n954:   (`parity_test.cljc:99`) and numeric store keys are part of the corpus\n990:| `:arity`          | the count differs from the tag's body arity plus one                                                                                              |\n997:| `:id-resolves`    | a child id in a `node` or `nodes` slot names no row of the loaded set                                                                             |\n1003:| `:variable-bounds`| a `:variable` name must be bound by an enclosing `:lambda`'s params, else the frontend must have emitted `:global`; the defect names the path     |\n1008:resolve within the loaded set and close under the root, as a jump target\n1020:dense pcs, sorted by pc, refs resolve to entities) are satisfied by the\n1031:| `:arity`         | the tuple's count differs from the mnemonic's arity in `yin.vm.semantic.md` §2.4 as saturated by UCF §7.3.2                                         |\n1034:|                  | a `:var` name or a `:global` name is not a symbol, a `:closure` params is not a vector of symbols, a `:ffi-call` op or `:resume` parked id is not a keyword, a `:gensym`  |\n1061:index, or a projection while stepping. Projection and query are load-time\n1079:;; :global rows are exactly the free names; :variable rows carry a name too, but a bound one contributes no obligation (§7.7.2)\n1175:| `:variable`,  | `:closure`, `:push`,   | a call's effects   |                                                                                                          |\n1189:#### 7.7.2 Name obligations are resolved per store slice, and completion is conservative\n1191:A name extracted from code (a `:global` row) is an **obligation**. Because this design preserves named variables across the Semantic Tuple boundary, the evaluator simply looks up the name in the environment.\n1193:**Variables never fall through to globals.** An under-arity call leaves missing parameter names bound to `nil`; an over-arity call drops extra arguments beyond the params list length. An unbound variable name evaluates to `nil`; it never falls through to the store, primitives, or modules (since `:variable` and `:global` are distinct nodes). Therefore, name obligations are strictly and statically the set of `:global` names, never `:variable` names.\n1205:sentence that a name \"is satisfied if it is bound in any environment the\n1214:environments are two work items, because each enters the segment with its\n1215:own environment (`semantic.cljc:199-205`) and so reaches different values (closures, streams, cursors, parked records), which\n1217:closure's captured environment, and nothing else. This context\n1245:as a profiled primitive or module requirement, every parked id resolved, and every module\n1354:(`datom.md:200-212`) and a composition cannot mint one. Where a\n1355:composition wants an event to be the provenance of a naming fact, the\n1368:The vocabulary is open: a composition that needs a new op declares a new\n1435:enforced by how the transactor resolves ids: `apply-tempid-map` replaces a\n1442:  batch member index: the successor of `:yin/source-call` qualified by\n1443:  `:yin/source-batch`, which no transactor resolves, as today;\n1447:  parent event's id, the successor of `:yin/source-node` and resolved by\n1491:  cursor is a position minted by the stream for observation\n1495:  with no append between them read one position. Nor does committing a\n1500:  are already resolved (`src/cljc/dao/space/transactor.cljc:231-254`);\n1504:  **composition-minted token**, the one mechanism for every construction:\n1513:  The uniqueness warranty is the composition's, discharged by the token's\n1519:  being avoided. No id allocated by any transactor, and no position of\n1557:disconnected definition, so the composition between frontend and expander\n1562: :yin/root          i                                ; index of the tree the evaluator runs\n1574:  resolved batch; nothing requires entity order to equal structural\n1621:  declaration ordinal `k` is its index in the declaration catalogue, never\n1622:  its index in the harvest catalogue; every occurrence of that group is\n1648:  declaration whose coordinates do not resolve to such a node is an\n1657:  admitted position becomes the declaration at that tree and path. The\n1673:- **Evaluators see the root only.** The composition hands an evaluator\n1684:which resolves the greatest `t` per `[e a v]` and then removes retractions\n1695:(`query/current` two-arity, `query.cljc:210-212`; `bound-datoms`,\n1726:The walker stays on map ASTs exactly as built, retaining named variable evaluation. What changes is the\n1733:| walker, `ast_walker.cljc`                        | Retains named variable evaluation (`:name`). `:lambda` arm binds by name. Does not use De Bruijn numbering. Adds `:stream/close` arm (§3.2).                                                                                                      |\n1738:| linearizer,                                      | reads the row relation through the same `get-attr`-over-an-index shape it has today (`lower-node`'s `(get-attr e    |\n1739:| `linearize.cljc:87-148`,                         | :yin/type)` becomes a lookup by row id); `ast-children` becomes a table lookup of `node`/`nodes` slot positions;    |\n1740:| `:230-242`                                       | `lower` takes a row set and returns a vector plus the §5.3 provenance table; emits `:var name`, `:global name`, and `:closure params body`; `lower-ast` (`:245-252`) goes away     |\n1743:|                                                  | `:yin/root` and `:eid` removed; `:yin/address` added; `:global` node added; retains `:yin/params` on lambda and `:yin/name` on variable |\n1748:| `semantic/load-image`,                           | decodes from the vector directly on the primary path; frame binding for `:closure` matches arguments to `params` by position, binding each to its name (§7.7.2); `:global` opcode resolves store → primitives → modules; decodes the new operands (`:var name`, `:global name`, `:closure params body`); both paths call the §7.5 validator   |\n1756:|                                                  | a declaration at its tree index and path, then strip the flag                                                       |\n1773:composition-supplied `load`. The per-evaluator loaders are chosen in\n1794:  composition reaches the predicate is what the implementation phase\n1807:- **`dao.space.index` and published covered indexes**: they index datoms,\n1843:   composition names its program medium by; this document does not fix\n1845:   written. The expander incarnation (§8.4.1) is a composition-minted\n1846:   random token, never a log-allocated id or a stream position; its\n1847:   uniqueness is the composition's warranty, discharged by the token's\n1870:   captured-environment context abstraction for values. Neither analysis exists in code;\n1880:   any-carried-environment satisfaction sentence is unsound and must be\n1881:   replaced by the store-slice-by-key / profile rule of §7.7.2 (an environment never\n1914:    Named variable instruction grammar\n1915:    and the argument-to-named-parameter binding rule of §7.7.2 (arguments match `params` by position, each bound to its name; under-arity call → missing parameter names bound to `nil`; extra arguments beyond the params list length are droppe